{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012NBvq3fWGKaBTScLuoetUU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"E2 didn't fire. Let me investigate why. Let me check the `advance_to_phase` implementation and the `advance_phase` method more carefully.\n\nLooking at `advance_to_phase`, it calls `game.advance_phase()` multiple times. Let me check if the PRECOMBAT_MAIN triggers happen when advancing.\n\nWait, I need to check the condition. `advance_to_phase` calls `game.advance_phase()` repeatedly. Let me check if the event fires when the phase becomes PRECOMBAT_MAIN.\n\nBut the issue is that my code fires the event AFTER `empty_mana_pools()`. \n\nThe trigger goes to the stack, but `advance_to_phase` doesn't run the priority loop—it just advances until the target phase is reached. Let me trace through what happens: starting from BEGINNING/UNTAP, each call to `advance_phase()` moves forward and fires the corresponding triggered events like BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent and BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent. The function checks if `(game.phase, game.step) == target` after each advance, so I need to verify the exact sequence of when the event fires versus when the phase check happens.\n\nThe test starts with the game at BEGINNING/UNTAP, then calls `advance_to_phase(game2, Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN)` where the target becomes `(Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None)`. The initial position is `(Phase.BEGINNING, Step.UNTAP)`, and I'm checking how the turn sequence progresses from there.\n\nLooking at the turn sequence, PRECOMBAT_MAIN is at index 3, so it takes 3 calls to `advance_phase()` to reach it. The `advance_phase` method increments through the sequence, updates the phase and step, empties mana pools, and then fires the PRECOMBAT_MAIN event when that phase is reached.\n\nThe problem is that the trigger gets pushed to the stack when the event fires, but `advance_to_phase` never runs the priority loop or resolves anything on the stack. So the trigger's effect lambda—which is what actually appends to `fired2`—never executes because the trigger never resolves.\n\nI should verify this by checking if the trigger is actually sitting on the stack, then either resolve it or rewrite the test to check the stack directly instead of relying on the effect callback.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1103,"cache_read_input_tokens":96410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1103},"output_tokens":31,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"f137b14d-8b0d-43b5-bf7b-53db0b28da44","request_id":"req_011Cbw9eXgse6Xc7yCZFE2kX"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012NBvq3fWGKaBTScLuoetUU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019vqFGwyN4f7yavRvCLabdT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom test_utils import create_game, advance_to_phase\nfrom engine.types import Phase, Zone\nfrom engine.events import BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent\nfrom engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\nfrom engine.state_based_actions import resolve_state_based_actions\n\n# E2 test: BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent fires on advance_phase to PRECOMBAT_MAIN\ngame2 = create_game()\np1 = game2.players[0]\nfired2 = []\ngame2.trigger_manager.register(TriggerRegistration(\n    event_type=BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent,\n    condition=None,\n    effect=lambda g: fired2.append(1),\n    source=object(),\n    controller=p1,\n))\nadvance_to_phase(game2, Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN)\nprint('Stack size after advance:', len(game2.stack))\n# Resolve the stack\nwhile not game2.stack.is_empty():\n    obj = game2.stack.pop()\n    obj.on_resolve(game2)\n    resolve_state_based_actions(game2)\nprint('fired2:', fired2)\nassert len(fired2) > 0\nprint('E2 OK: trigger fires and resolves when advancing to PRECOMBAT_MAIN')\n\n# Also verify mana added in trigger survives (it's after empty_mana_pools)\nfrom engine.types import ManaType\ngame3 = create_game()\np1 = game3.players[0]\ngame3.trigger_manager.register(TriggerRegistration(\n    event_type=BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent,\n    condition=None,\n    effect=lambda g: g.players[0].mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, 3),\n    source=object(),\n    controller=p1,\n))\nadvance_to_phase(game3, Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN)\n# The trigger is on the stack - resolve it\nwhile not game3.stack.is_empty():\n    obj = game3.stack.pop()\n    obj.on_resolve(game3)\nprint('Mana after trigger resolves:', p1.mana_pool.total())\nassert p1.mana_pool.total() == 3, f'Expected 3, got {p1.mana_pool.total()}'\nprint('E2 OK: mana added by trigger survives into main phase')\n\"\n","description":"Verify E2 with stack resolution"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1103,"cache_read_input_tokens":96410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1103},"output_tokens":31,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"9e360d3f-840e-4175-92fa-e8247c0925ea","request_id":"req_011Cbw9eXgse6Xc7yCZFE2kX"}
