{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_016mUAWTsgk5xNPe1o1x2Thy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have everything I need. Let me implement sos_4 — Together as One.\n\nCard spec:\n- Name: \"Together as One\"\n- Mana cost: {6}\n- Type: Sorcery\n- Oracle text: \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\n\nImplementation:\n- `on_resolve`: X = len(set(card.colors_spent))\n- Draws X cards for target player\n- Deals X damage to any target\n- Caster gains X life\n\nI need to handle two separate targets in `get_targets()`: one for the target player and another for any target (player or creature). The engine will iterate through the TargetRequirements list and prompt for each one.\n\nIn `on_resolve`, `chosen_targets[0]` will be the player who draws, and `chosen_targets[1]` will be the damage target. I should also account for X being zero and handle cases where `colors_spent` might not be set if the spell was cast for free. For the \"any target\" filter, I need to accept both players and creatures based on their attributes.\n\nDefining the card class... Implementing the spell resolution logic... Looking at how the casting pipeline validates targets, it checks the `filter_fn` if provided but doesn't actually validate against the `zone` parameter—that seems to be more informational about where targeting applies. For the Refute spell specifically, it's using `zone=Zone.STACK` with a filter that checks for specific object types.\n\nI'm realizing I need to clarify what attributes distinguish players from creatures in the engine—players have `life` but creatures have `damage_marked` instead, so the filter function needs to account for this difference when accepting \"any target.\" For gaining life directly, I need to increment the controller's life total and fire a GainsLifeTriggeredEvent, similar to how the engine handles it in other cards.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the edge cases: when X is 0 (from colorless mana or no colors spent), drawing and dealing damage both handle that gracefully, and gaining 0 life is fine too. The target player could be the caster or their opponent, which the function should support either way.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1062,"cache_read_input_tokens":103441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1062},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"2ff57046-64eb-4234-b304-26dc4f21f286","request_id":"req_011Cbw9jTUWPgLFSgvqpRRHY"}
