{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01RHkrJyaqFuxUew8tsGwVnL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see now that `declare_attackers_step` in combat.py is called from the turn loop, but it doesn't fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent`. The turn loop calls `priority_loop` after each step.\n\nLooking at the combat flow:\n1. DECLARE_ATTACKERS step: `declare_attackers_step(game)` is called, which calls `active.choose(eligible, \"declare attackers\")` to get the list of attackers, sets them as attacking, and taps them.\n2. Then `priority_loop(game)` is called.\n\nBut `AttacksTriggeredEvent` is never actually fired during gameplay—it's defined and registered in cards but never triggered by the combat step. This is a bug in the engine, and there aren't even tests for attack-triggered abilities in the FDN test suite, so it's been an untested gap.\n\nThe TODO comment suggests these cards should reuse the existing seam by registering triggers on `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, which means the event is supposed to fire. I need to add the event firing to `declare_attackers_step` in the combat module—after each attacker is declared, I'll fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` with the creature and attacker parameters. This is a necessary engine fix to make attack triggers work at all.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2916,"cache_read_input_tokens":134530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2916},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"6143dc15-8e37-4579-95cb-ce6879687f91","request_id":"req_011CbwAAwPEUoXXyW1RL7TCN"}
