{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01QwzVUxqMy4wdzkuczBfVfb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The conftest.py doesn't help with triggers. The issue is clear: `set_board_state` places cards directly in zones without calling `register_triggers`. I need to call `archaic.register_triggers(game)` in my test.\n\nLet me update the test to call `register_triggers` after placing the archaic on the battlefield. Or better: I can use `move_to_zone` to properly place it, or I can just call `register_triggers` manually.\n\nActually looking at how other test cards use `set_board_state`... they just do it. The FDN tests with creatures don't test attack triggers.\nI'm realizing that other attack-triggered cards in FDN don't have tests either, so this is a known gap. The proper approach would be using `move_to_zone` since that automatically registers triggers, but `set_board_state` bypasses that. For now, I'll manually call `register_triggers` after setting up the board state. I could also use `move_to_zone` to put the creature on the battlefield, which would automatically register triggers, but that might fire ETB effects I don't want. The simpler approach is to call `register_triggers` directly after `set_board_state`, making sure the controller is set properly first.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":648,"cache_read_input_tokens":140204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":648},"output_tokens":33,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"63c226bb-dbbc-4675-b9dd-82f885822a8c","request_id":"req_011CbwADymwDqPEDUYgwbpks"}
