{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011kiAZaeXeZFkuBegkcED38","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the land pattern. For sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex, I need to:\n\n1. Two mana abilities:\n   - `{T}`: Add {C}\n   - `{T}, Pay 1 life`: Add one mana of any color, restricted to instant/sorcery spells\n\n2. Activated ability: `{5}`: If not already a creature, become a 2/4 Wizard creature (still a land) with \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery, +1/+0 until EOT\"\n   \nFor the restricted mana, I need to add a lightweight restriction marker to the mana pool so that certain mana can only be used for specific spell types. The current `ManaPool` is just a simple dictionary tracking mana counts, so I'll need to extend it to track which mana has restrictions and validate those restrictions when paying for spells.\n\nThe minimal approach is to add a `_restricted_mana` dictionary to `ManaPool` that tracks mana with restrictions by type, then enforce these restrictions during the payment phase when casting non-instant/sorcery spells. _spell` spells. The key insight is to keep restricted mana separate from the main pool so it only counts toward instant/sorcery casting, avoiding the need to modify payment logic at every call site.\n\nThe challenge is that `can_pay` and `pay` don't know the spell type, so I need to either pass that information through or temporarily adjust the pool before payment. The simpler approach is to remove restricted mana from the pool before calling `can_pay`/`pay` for non-instant/sorcery spells, then restore it afterward.\n\nWriting the implementation... Adding the restricted mana to the normal pool when casting instant/sorcery spells, but keeping it unavailable otherwise, is the cleanest approach. I'll add a separate tracking mechanism for instant/sorcery-only mana and have `cast_spell` conditionally make it available based on the spell type. but marked with a restriction so it can only be used for instants and sorceries. The engine needs to track this restricted mana separately in the pool—I'll add a dictionary to store restricted mana by type, then modify the payment logic so that non-instant/sorcery spells can only draw from the unrestricted pool, while instants and sorceries can use both.\n\nThe tricky part is that `can_pay` and `pay` don't currently know what type of spell is being cast, so I need a way to unlock the restricted mana temporarily when paying for instants or sorceries. I could either add a spell type parameter to those methods or use a simpler approach: call `unlock_restricted()` before paying for an instant/sorcery to move the restricted amounts into the main pool, then `lock_restricted()` afterward to move any leftovers back. This keeps the existing method signatures clean without breaking the API.\n\nThe card ability creates mana that can only be spent on instants or sorceries, so I'll track this as a separate `_restricted_for_instant_sorcery` dictionary in the mana pool. When casting an instant or sorcery, I temporarily merge the restricted mana into the available pool for payment, then restore what's left. For other spell types, the restricted mana stays locked and unusable. This requires updates to both the mana pool class and the casting logic. Continuing with the mana pool implementation...\n\nI'm finishing the unlock method to transfer restricted mana back into the main pool, then clearing both pools in the empty method. When casting an instant or sorcery spell, I check the card type and unlock the restricted mana so it becomes available for payment. Clearing the restricted mana pools in the `empty()` method. Now for the animation ability, I need to gate it on the card not already being a creature, then add the creature type and Wizard subtype with 2/4 stats, plus register a trigger for the pump effect that grants +1/+0 until end of turn.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1179,"cache_read_input_tokens":158141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1179},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"7f627c1b-8788-456c-b391-8265a6263d91","request_id":"req_011CbwAXCwRf2g2SNd1cMy6B"}
