{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\nThe user invoked the `execute-todo` skill to implement 10 SOS cards in a Magic: The Gathering game engine workspace. The skill reads `/workspace/TODO.md` and `/workspace/CONTEXT.md` and implements cards one at a time through the real engine. The cards to implement are: sos_1, sos_4, sos_13, sos_57, sos_97, sos_120, sos_201, sos_226, sos_245, sos_257. The plan requires 3 shared engine changes first (E1-E3), then 10 card implementations in dependency order. Approach: surgical additive reuse — reuse existing engine seams, keep changes small and card-local, always run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` before committing. All changes must be additive-only (no renames/deletes in engine/).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n- MTG game engine in Python with engine/ directory\n- CardImpl base class with hooks: cost_reduction, on_resolve, get_targets, register_triggers, register_replacement_effects, get_activated_abilities\n- Triggered abilities: TriggerRegistration + TriggerManager.register/fire_event\n- Replacement effects: ReplacementEffect + ReplacementManager\n- Zone system: Zone enum (BATTLEFIELD, HAND, LIBRARY, GRAVEYARD, EXILE, STACK)\n- SpellCastTriggeredEvent, BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent, AttacksTriggeredEvent, DrawsCardTriggeredEvent, BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent\n- cast_spell / cast_spell_free for free-cast from any zone\n- copy_spell for spell copies (casualty, paradigm)\n- _exile_instead_of_graveyard flag approach for stack→graveyard redirect\n- E3: spell_cost_reduction(game, spell) hook on battlefield permanents\n- Keyword flags: FLYING, DEATHTOUCH, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE\n- Converge: X = len(set(card.colors_spent))\n- Affinity for creatures: cost_reduction counts creatures you control\n- Casualty: sacrifice creature with power >= 1 to copy a spell\n- ManaPool with color tracking, can_pay/pay methods\n- ContinuousEffect for until-EOT effects (Layer 7c, DURATION_END_OF_TURN)\n- DeterministicPlayer with _script deque for scripted choices in tests\n- set_board_state doesn't call register_triggers (tests must do it manually)\n- AttacksTriggeredEvent was never fired in engine — fixed by adding it to declare_attackers_step\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n- **engine/casting.py** (modified):\n  - Added SpellCastTriggeredEvent firing after stack.push in cast_spell (E1)\n  - Extended get_cost_reduction to aggregate spell_cost_reduction from battlefield permanents for instant/sorcery (E3)\n  - Added _exile_instead_of_graveyard flag check in _resolve_spell:\n    ```python\n    if getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False):\n        card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = False\n        move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.EXILE)\n    else:\n        move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n    ```\n\n- **engine/events.py** (modified):\n  - Added BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent before BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent:\n    ```python\n    @dataclass\n    class BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n        pass\n    ```\n\n- **engine/game_state.py** (modified):\n  - Added event firing in advance_phase after empty_mana_pools():\n    ```python\n    if self.phase == Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN:\n        from engine.events import BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent\n        self.trigger_manager.fire_event(self, BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent())\n    ```\n\n- **engine/combat.py** (modified):\n  - Added AttacksTriggeredEvent firing after declaring all attackers in declare_attackers_step:\n    ```python\n    from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n    for attacker in combat.attackers:\n        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n            game,\n            AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker),\n        )\n    ```\n\n- **cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py** (implemented):\n  - TogetherAsOne(Sorcery), mana_cost={6}\n  - get_targets: returns 2 TargetRequirements (target player, any target)\n  - on_resolve: X = len(set(colors_spent)), draws X for target, deals X damage, gains X life\n  \n- **cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py** (created): 4 tests passing\n\n- **cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py** (implemented):\n  - TheDawningArchaic(Creature), mana_cost={10}, 7/7 Legendary Avatar\n  - keywords: Keyword.REACH\n  - cost_reduction: counts instant/sorcery in controller's graveyard\n  - register_triggers: AttacksTriggeredEvent trigger → choose_card from graveyard instant/sorcery → cast free → set _exile_instead_of_graveyard = True\n\n- **cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py** (created): 7 tests passing\n\n- **cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py** (implemented):\n  - WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature), mana_cost={6}{B}{G}, 5/5 Legendary Elder Dragon\n  - keywords: Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH\n  - cost_reduction: counts creatures you control (self-affinity)\n  - spell_cost_reduction(game, spell): E3 hook, returns creature count for controller's spells only\n\n- **cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py** (created): 6 tests passing\n\n- **cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py** (implemented):\n  - SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature), mana_cost={2}{W}{B}, 4/4 Legendary Elder Dragon\n  - keywords: Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.VIGILANCE\n  - register_triggers: SpellCastTriggeredEvent → casualty (choose_card for sacrifice, sacrifice if power>=1, copy_spell + push):\n    ```python\n    def _condition(g, event):\n        if event.controller is not source.controller: return False\n        card_types = getattr(event.card, \"card_types\", set())\n        return CardType.INSTANT in card_types or CardType.SORCERY in card_types\n    ```\n\n- **cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py** (created): 5 tests passing\n\n- **KEY_DECISIONS.md** (created): documents _exile_instead_of_graveyard, AttacksTriggeredEvent fix, E3 approach\n\n- **engine/continuous_effects.py** (read): ContinuousEffect dataclass with Layer enum, SubLayer, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0, DURATION_PERMANENT=-1\n\n- **engine/mana.py** (read): ManaPool with _pool dict, add, empty, can_pay, pay, _restricted_inst_sorc not yet added\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n\n- **sos_4 test: Zone lookup with string key**: Test used `player.zones['hand']` instead of `player.zones[Zone.HAND]`. Fixed by using Zone enum.\n\n- **E2 smoke test: BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent appeared not to fire**: The trigger IS pushed to the stack (fire_event pushes a StackObject), but the test checked `fired2` list which is only populated when the trigger's `on_resolve` is called. The trigger was on the stack unresolved. Fixed by resolving the stack in the test (`_resolve_top_of_stack`).\n\n- **sos_1 test: attack trigger not firing**: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined in events.py and registered by many cards, but NEVER fired in the engine's `declare_attackers_step`. This was a fundamental engine bug affecting all attack-triggered cards. Fixed by adding the `fire_event` loop to `declare_attackers_step` in `engine/combat.py`.\n\n- **sos_1 test: triggers not registered**: `set_board_state` places cards directly in zones without calling `register_triggers`. The Dawning Archaic's attack trigger was never registered. Fixed by adding `archaic.register_triggers(game)` call in tests after `set_board_state`.\n\n- **sos_226 test: casualty no-power test**: Test assumed no sacrifice prompt when only a 0/5 wall was on battlefield alongside Silverquill (power 4 >= 1). But Silverquill itself is a sacrificeable creature. Fixed by changing test to test sorcery casualty instead, which is a valid meaningful test.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n- Engine gap: AttacksTriggeredEvent never fired → added to declare_attackers_step\n- Replacement effects don't apply for stack→graveyard moves → used _exile_instead_of_graveyard flag approach (deliberate limitation: doesn't handle countered spells)\n- set_board_state bypasses register_triggers → tests must call register_triggers manually after set_board_state for triggered creatures\n- E3: spell_cost_reduction hook on permanent allows battlefield permanents to reduce instant/sorcery spell costs without adding per-spell edits\n\n6. All user messages:\n- \"Run the `execute-todo` skill now to implement the SOS cards. Your task and prepared execution plan are in /workspace/TODO.md and /workspace/CONTEXT.md.\"\n- The skill instructions (full execute-todo skill text) instructing: orient once, work items in order, read specs and mirror FDN analogues, test through real engine, run engine_tests after each card, mark checkboxes, commit per card, write KEY_DECISIONS.md for ambiguous decisions, never stop to ask questions.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n- [ ] sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex (currently in progress — reading continuous_effects.py when summary was requested)\n- [ ] sos_57 — Mana Sculpt (counter + E2 delayed mana)\n- [ ] sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone (cast-from-exile + Paradigm + E2)\n- [ ] sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares (ETB token + Prepared state + cast-from-exile)\n- [ ] sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian (Flying+Haste + Miracle + loot trigger)\n- [ ] sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer (Planeswalker + Surveil + coin-flip + skip-turns)\n\n8. Current Work:\nImmediately before this summary, the implementation of **sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex** was being planned. The agent had:\n1. Read `engine/continuous_effects.py` to understand ContinuousEffect, Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0 (for pump until EOT)\n2. Read `cards/fdn/fdn_267/card_impl.py` (Secluded Courtyard) showing the land+mana ability pattern with `get_mana_abilities()` returning `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` list, with a tap_cost function pattern\n3. Was planning to:\n   - Add restricted mana support to `engine/mana.py` (new field `_restricted_inst_sorc: dict[ManaType, int]`, new method `add_restricted_instant_sorcery`, updated `empty()`, and `unlock_for_instant_sorcery()` to merge into main pool)\n   - Modify `cast_spell` in casting.py to call `unlock_for_instant_sorcery()` before payment for instant/sorcery spells\n   - Implement `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)` with two mana abilities and one activated ability (animation)\n\nThe card spec for sos_257:\n```\n{T}: Add {C}.\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\n{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.\n```\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\nContinue implementing sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex. The next concrete step is to:\n\n1. Add restricted mana support to `engine/mana.py`:\n   - Add `_restricted_inst_sorc: dict[ManaType, int]` field to `ManaPool.__init__`\n   - Add `add_restricted_instant_sorcery(mana_type, amount=1)` method\n   - Add `unlock_for_instant_sorcery()` method that merges restricted mana into `_pool`\n   - Update `empty()` to also clear `_restricted_inst_sorc`\n\n2. Modify `cast_spell` in `engine/casting.py` to call `player.mana_pool.unlock_for_instant_sorcery()` before the `can_pay`/`pay` calls when the spell is an instant/sorcery\n\n3. Write `cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py`:\n   - `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)` with two mana abilities (`get_mana_abilities()`) and one activated ability (`get_activated_abilities()`)\n   - Animation activated ability (`{5}` cost): gate on `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types`, add CREATURE type, set base_power=2/base_toughness=4, add \"Wizard\" subtype, register SpellCastTriggeredEvent pump trigger (+1/+0 until EOT via ContinuousEffect with DURATION_END_OF_TURN)\n\n4. Write tests in `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`\n\n5. Run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` to verify no regressions\n\n6. Commit: `git add -A && git commit -m \"sos_257: Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"`\n\nThis is directly in line with the execute-todo skill instruction: \"Work the items **in order, one at a time**\" and sos_257 is the next unchecked item after sos_226.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"b6a6b2cf-a04f-4c73-a829-b548578b66b6","timestamp":"2026-06-11T08:37:34.654Z","isSynthetic":true}
