{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Pwz3TdXVFoTZqTN5fSxZTf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `_reset_characteristics()` resets `card_types` to `_original_card_types`. This means if I just mutate `card_types`, it will be reset next time `apply_all` is called.\n\nTo make the animation permanent, I need to ALSO update `_original_card_types` (to include CREATURE) so that resets preserve the animation. This is the correct approach:\n1. When the animation activates:\n   - `self.card_types |= {CardType.CREATURE}`\n   - `self._original_card_types = frozenset(self.card_types)` — update baseline\n2. Also update the power, toughness, and add Wizard to the subtypes\n\nAlternatively, I could use a ContinuousEffect with DURATION_PERMANENT to handle this more cleanly through the layer system — adding CREATURE on Layer.TYPE and adjusting power/toughness on the appropriate layers. That approach would integrate better with how the engine handles permanent modifications.\n\nThe tricky part is that this land doesn't inherit from Creature, so it won't have the standard `_reset_characteristics` method that creatures use to manage their P/T. I need to check how Creature handles this reset to understand what I'm missing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":836,"cache_read_input_tokens":60231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":836},"output_tokens":35,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"4bf2e182-5baf-4afa-8847-9192ab3ea18b","request_id":"req_011CbwAtXfPWr3KWSzQoUagq"}
