{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JsSaB8HAf7f8DYCSDr5bBG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see. The Land class doesn't have `base_power`, `modified_power` etc. I need a Land that can become a Creature. The cleanest approach is:\n\n1. Have `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex` extend `Land`, not `Creature`. It starts as just a land.\n2. In `__init__`, add creature-like attributes (`base_power`, `base_toughness`, `modified_power`, `modified_toughness`, `damage_marked`, etc.) so it can behave as a creature when animated.\n3. When animated, I'll use a permanent continuous effect to add CREATURE and the Wizard subtype to the card's types, while also setting the base power and toughness. This avoids the issue of Land not having `_reset_characteristics` by storing the effect permanently rather than trying to mutate the card type directly.\n\nActually, the simpler approach is to just mutate `_original_card_types` and set the base power/toughness attributes directly when the animation fires—no continuous effect needed. I'll add CREATURE to the card types, set base_power and base_toughness to 2 and 4, and mark the card as animated with a flag.\n\nFor the SpellCast trigger that pumps the creature with +1/+0 until end of turn, I need `modified_power` to exist on the card so the effect can increment it. I'll pre-initialize both `modified_power` and `modified_toughness` in the constructor even though the card starts as a land, so they're ready when the pump effect applies.\n\nInitializing creature attributes... Writing the ability effect... Writing the card implementation... Continuing the class initialization...\n\nI'm setting up the mana ability methods, starting with a tap cost function that checks if the source is already tapped, then defining a variant that also costs a life point from the controller. I'm also creating effect functions for generating colorless mana and any-color mana to the controller's