{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01FQkuS9uRcA8nQroivvwbU8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I have a clear picture. Let me also check the `ActivatedAbility` cost signature to ensure it matches what I'm expecting. Looking at fdn_114, the cost is `def _cost(game, src)` and it gets called as `ability.cost(game, ability.source)` in `_activate_regular_ability`.\n\nBut wait - for the animation activated ability, I need the land to not be on the stack/casting - it's an ability activation. The cost callback is `(game, src) -> bool`. Looking at fdn_114:\n- `_cost(game, src)` receives `src = ability.source = the card`\n- Uses `src.controller` to get the player\n\nGood, the pattern is consistent.\n\nBut there's another issue: the `{5}` cost check. Looking at fdn_114, I see how mana costs are validated and paid - checking the total available mana and specific color requirements, then calling the pay method. For `{5}`, I just need to verify the controller has at least 5 total mana available and then pay it.\n\nNow thinking through the animation test flow: when I call `activate_ability`, it triggers the cost check and then the effect. The pump trigger only registers after the animation completes, so I need to sequence the test properly - animate the land first, then cast a spell to fire the trigger. Since `_activate_regular_ability` pushes to the stack, the animation effect itself resolves as a StackObject, which means I need to trace through how that resolution works.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":709,"cache_read_input_tokens":66527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":709},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-