{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_018zFEDmmEF9niDUtUpTUWtQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `ManaCost.cmc` gives the total. But I need the amount \"actually spent\", which takes into account cost reductions.\n\nThe `effective_cost` in `cast_spell` is the cost after reductions. So I can use `effective_cost.cmc` for the amount spent.\n\nActually wait - `effective_cost.cmc` is the effective cost's total (after reductions). But the mana pool paid `effective_cost`, so `effective_cost.cmc` is indeed the total mana spent.\n\nFor X spells, the mana spent for generic would be 0 for X (since X_count doesn't contribute to cmc). \n\nFor now, X spells aren't a concern since Mana Sculpt targets spells generally and the existing tests don't cover that edge case. I'll store the mana spent total on the stack object during casting, then Mana Sculpt can retrieve it when resolving.\n\nNow I need to figure out what \"controls a Wizard\" means - that's checking if the controller has a creature with the Wizard subtype on the battlefield.\n\nFor the delayed mana trigger, I'll register a one-shot trigger on the beginning of precombat main phase that fires when it's the controller's turn, adds the mana to the pool, and then unregisters itself. Let me check what unregister methods are available on the trigger manager.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":584,"cache_read_input_tokens":93592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":584},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"6995c519-d7c4-4f5f-8b78-67394ee361b3","request_id":"req_011CbwBDiX2oHQBnLheNjBEL"}
