{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012tETb2k2ZA1kZu88PLVpRD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's `unregister(source)` which removes all triggers for a source. But for Mana Sculpt's one-shot trigger, I need to track the trigger registration itself and remove it after it fires. I can use a closure variable.\n\nBut actually, `unregister(source)` takes a source, and for a transient trigger like the delayed mana, the \"source\" is the Mana Sculpt card itself. But Mana Sculpt goes to the graveyard after resolving... So after the trigger fires at the beginning of next main phase, I can call `game.trigger_manager.unregister(source)` where source is the Mana Sculpt card.\nEach Mana Sculpt instance is a different object, so even if I cast it multiple times, unregistering by the card object would only remove that specific trigger. The cleaner approach is to use a mutable container that holds the trigger registration, then the effect function can access and remove it when the trigger fires. I'm realizing the issue with unregistering by source — it would remove all triggers tied to that card, which could be problematic if the same Mana Sculpt somehow gets cast multiple times. The safer approach is using a `TriggerRegistration` holder to remove just the specific trigger instance.\n\nNow I need to add `mana_spent_total` to the StackObject dataclass in the `cast_spell` method.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2172,"cache_read_input_tokens":94176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2172},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"5ca4ca52-1694-4e77-b8d4-3bdc5c2f090b","request_id":"req_011CbwBEbTu9k