{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01CABj8L7mpTuWMbaQj7EsAu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `library.top(n)` returns the top n items. The library is ordered bottom-to-top, so the last item is the \"top of the library\". That means `top(1)` returns `[top_card]` and `top_card` is `library.top(1)[-1]`.\n\nFor exiling cards from top of library:\n- I need to peek one at a time and check mana value\n- `card.mana_cost.cmc` for mana value (treating X as 0 is fine)\n- Keep going until total MV >= 4\n\nThen for \"you may cast any number of them without paying their mana costs\":\n- I'll iterate through the exiled cards and let the player choose which ones to cast for free, skipping any lands since they can't be cast that way\n\nFor the Paradigm effect, I need to handle this differently: after the Capstone resolves and exiles itself, I'll set up a recurring trigger that fires at the beginning of each of the controller's main phases. Each time it triggers, I create a copy of the Capstone in exile and offer the player to cast that copy for free. I need to be careful about infinite recursion here—when the copy resolves, it'll trigger the same ability again. I should probably track whether this is the original spell or a copy to prevent that loop, or set up the trigger differently so it only fires once per turn rather than creating new triggers each time. the copy doesn't exile itself because the Paradigm ability only registers once on the original card. When copies resolve from exile, they just go to the graveyard normally without triggering the exile-instead effect again. So the loop stops naturally—the recurring trigger keeps casting copies, but those copies don't create new Paradigm triggers or exile themselves. they also exile themselves per the same rule, but the recurring trigger only registers once from the first resolution. So each copy that resolves exiles itself and stays in exile, while the trigger continues to fire each main phase, letting the player cast another copy. I'm tracking this with a flag on the spell to handle the exile behavior and the one-time trigger registration. I'll use a flag on the controller to track whether the paradigm trigger has been registered, checking it before registration to avoid duplicates. The recurring trigger fires at the beginning of each of my first main phases indefinitely, and when the copy resolves, it sets the exile flag but doesn't re-register the trigger itself.\n\nFor the casting mechanic, I'll iterate through the exiled cards and skip any that can't be cast like lands, then prompt the player for each castable card using a simple yes/no choice that can be scripted for the DeterministicPlayer.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":650,"cache_read_input_tokens":106349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":650},"output_tokens":35,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"de868c2c-bf80-4622-88f2-13f6fcfa5829","request_id":"req_011CbwBQNVa4RmDUqs8Uqia5"}
