{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Q1CVmrs5zGexRX2tUoyPbv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The card spec says:\n- \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\" — the full name is the front//back combined\n- It's a Creature — Cat Cleric\n- When this creature enters: target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling creature token with flying\n- Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared\n- Prepared: while it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell (Swords to Plowshares). Doing so unprepares it.\n\nSo the \"spell\" it refers to is Swords to Plowshares — which is:\n- Exiles target creature and its controller gains life equal to that creature's power\n- Costs just one white mana\n\nNow I need to implement this: create the Swords to Plowshares instant class, then build the creature with its ETB trigger that makes the token and checks if I need to set the prepared state, plus the prepared ability that lets me cast the spell.\n\nThe prepared mechanic is where I'm uncertain—whether it's an activated ability the player triggers manually, or something that happens automatically at the start of the main phase. The card text suggests it's something the player can do while prepared, but I need to figure out the exact activation mechanism.\n\nI'm leaning toward implementing it as an activated ability that checks if `_prepared` is true, then creates a copy of Swords to Plowshares, exiles it, casts it for free, and sets `_prepared` to false. This would be gated by the prepared state and available at sorcery speed.\n\nFor the token creation part, I need to handle the ETB trigger that creates a 1/1 Inkling token for a target player — the trigger fires when the card enters, and during resolution, the controller chooses which player gets the token via the targeting system.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage"