{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ApuUvZoKC2L66nxFMSoERz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\t## E1 — SpellCastTriggeredEvent placement\n4\tFired after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` in `cast_spell`. This matches the rule\n5\tthat the trigger fires once the spell is on the stack; it populates `spell`,\n6\t`card`, and `controller` from the cast_spell call.\n7\t\n8\t## E2 — BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent firing\n9\tFired in `GameState.advance_phase` after `empty_mana_pools()` so mana added by\n10\thandlers survives into the main phase. Using the inline lazy import to avoid\n11\tcircular imports.\n12\t\n13\t## sos_1 — AttacksTriggeredEvent never fired in engine\n14\t`AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined and registered by many cards but never fired by\n15\t`declare_attackers_step`. Added firing loop after declaring attackers in\n16\t`engine/combat.py`. This is an additive fix required for all attack-triggered cards.\n17\t\n18\t## sos_1 — _exile_instead_of_graveyard flag for stack→graveyard redirect\n19\tThe replacement effect system only applies for leaving-battlefield moves. For\n20\tinstants/sorceries going from stack to graveyard on resolution, added a\n21\t`_exile_instead_of_graveyard` attribute check in `_resolve_spell` (casting.py).\n22\tDeliberate limitation: does not apply when the spell is countered (counter bypasses\n23\t`_resolve_spell`).\n24\t\n25\t## E3 — Battlefield cost-reduction aggregation\n26\tExtends `get_cost_reduction` to aggregate `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)`\n27\tfrom the caster's battlefield permanents, but only for instant/sorcery spells.\n28\tThis is the minimal hook for Witherbloom's \"your instants/sorceries have affinity\n29\tfor creatures\" without building a general granted-keyword system.\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"5c58d7ee-0ae8-479d-ad98-b12cdf1afddf","timestamp":"2026-06-11T08:57:55.914Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","content":"# Key Decisions\n\n## E1 — SpellCastTriggeredEvent placement\nFired after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` in `cast_spell`. This matches the rule\nthat the trigger fires once the spell is on the stack; it populates `spell`,\n`card`, and `controller` from the cast_spell call.\n\n## E2 — BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent firing\nFired in `GameState.advance_phase` after `empty_mana_pools()` so mana added by\nhandlers survives into the main phase. Using the inline lazy import to avoid\ncircular imports.\n\n## sos_1 — AttacksTriggeredEvent never fired in engine\n`AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined and registered by many cards but never fired by\n`declare_attackers_step`. Added firing loop after declaring attackers in\n`engine/combat.py`. This is an additive fix required for all attack-triggered cards.\n\n## sos_1 — _exile_instead_of_graveyard flag for stack→graveyard redirect\nThe replacement effect system only applies for leaving-battlefield moves. For\ninstants/sorceries going from stack to graveyard on resolution, added a\n`_exile_instead_of_graveyard` attribute check in `_resolve_spell` (casting.py).\nDeliberate limitation: does not apply when the spell is countered (counter bypasses\n`_resolve_spell`).\n\n## E3 — Battlefield cost-reduction aggregation\nExtends `get_cost_reduction` to aggregate `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)`\nfrom the caster's battlefield permanents, but only for instant/sorcery spells.\nThis is the minimal hook for Witherbloom's \"your instants/sorceries have affinity\nfor creatures\" without building a general granted-keyword system.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Do2mytdHefBVdW95Bkrjnj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WwpZdmkiKZuehW9ZxjWCmY","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"## E3 — Battlefield cost-reduction aggregation\nExtends `get_cost_reduction` to aggregate `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)`\nfrom the caster's battlefield permanents, but only for instant/sorcery spells.\nThis is the minimal hook for Witherbloom's \"your instants/sorceries have affinity\nfor creatures\" without building a general granted-keyword system.","new_string":"## E3 — Battlefield cost-reduction aggregation\nExtends `get_cost_reduction` to aggregate `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)`\nfrom the caster's battlefield permanents, but only for instant/sorcery spells.\nThis is the minimal hook for Witherbloom's \"your instants/sorceries have affinity\nfor creatures\" without building a general granted-keyword system.\n\n## sos_257 — Great Hall restricted mana (ENGINE LIMITATION)\nThe \"{T}, Pay 1 life: Add any color, restricted to instant/sorcery\" mana is not\nenforced. The restriction marker is documented with an ENGINE LIMITATION comment,\nmirroring fdn_267 (Secluded Courtyard) which uses the same pattern.\n\n## sos_257 — Animation persists through reset\nWhen the land animates, both `card_types` and `_original_card_types` are updated.\nThis ensures the CREATURE type survives `EffectManager._reset_characteristics()` calls.\nThe pump trigger registers once inside the activated ability's effect.\n\n## sos_57 — mana_spent_total on StackObject\nAdded `stack_obj.mana_spent_total = effective_cost.cmc` in `cast_spell` after\npayment. Used by Mana Sculpt (and any future counterspell) to read the actual\nmana paid to cast the countered spell.\n\n## sos_120 — Paradigm registered once per player\nParadigm trigger is registered once via `controller._paradigm_capstone_registered`\nflag. Copies of the Capstone cast via Paradigm resolve normally but don't re-register\n(flag is already set). Copies also exile themselves via `_exile_instead_of_graveyard`.\n\n## sos_201 — Miracle first-draw tracking\nThe miracle condition sets `player._last_miracle_draw_turn = game.turn_number` inside\nthe condition function itself (before returning True). This ensures only the first\ndraw triggers miracle — subsequent draws in the same turn see the flag already set.\n\n## sos_97 — skip_turns engine change\nAdded skip_turns handling in `advance_phase` (game_state.py): when the next player\nhas `skip_turns > 0`, decrement and give the turn to the other player instead.\nDeliberate limitation: only handles 2-player games; extra_turns queue is unaffected.\n\n## sos_97 — game.rng for coin flips\nCoin flips use `getattr(game, \"rng\", None)` with fallback to `random.Random()`.\nTests set `game.rng` to a seeded or monkeypatched RNG for determinism."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":164549,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":702},"output_tokens":72,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad560dd-f0de-48bf-a5ec-5012d23eae4b","uuid":"dbd03fe4-793c-49d9-a337-7a55bc1f727a","request_id":"req_011CbwCJpBbt8oAhsh6yArCi"}
